{
  "title": "Tibial Shaft Stress Fractures",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3112/tibial-shaft-stress-fractures",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jan 29 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A tibial shaft stress fracture is an overuse injury where normal or abnormal bone is subjected to repetitive stress, resulting in microfractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can often be made on radiographs alone but MRI studies should be obtained in patients with normal radiographs with a high degree of suspicion for stress fracture.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is activity restriction with protected weight-bearing in most cases. Surgical intramedullary nailing is recommended in the presence of an anterior tibia tension-sided stress fracture (\"dreaded black line\").",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "commonly seen in runners and **military recruits**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "seen after change in training routine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "linear microfractures in trabecular bone from repetitive loading",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "callus formation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "woven bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "endochondral bone formation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "change in exercise routine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "onset of symptoms often insidious",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "symptoms initially worse with running, then may develop symptoms with daily activities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain directly over fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Radiographs**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lateral xray may show **\"dreaded black line\"** anteriorly indicating tension fracture from posterior muscle force",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3112/images/xray%20with%20dreaded%20black%20line.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows Tibial shaft stress fracture"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "endosteal thickening",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "periosteal reaction with cortical thickening",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Technetium Tc 99m bone scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "focal uptake in cortical and/or trabecular region",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**MRI**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**replacing bone scan** for diagnosis and is most sensitive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "marrow edema",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3112/images/mri%20-%20shows%20edema.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows Tibial Stress Fracture"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**earliest findings on T2-weighted images**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "periosteal high signal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "T1-weighted images show linear zone of low signal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity restriction with protected weightbearing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most cases",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "avoids NSAIDs (slows bone healing)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "consider bone stimulator",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "intramedullary tibial nailing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "if \"dreaded black line\" is present, especially if it violates the anterior cortex",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "fractures of anterior cortex of tibia have highest likelihood of delayed healing or non-union",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
